# What indexing a vocabulary costs: the first call of lpl::infer::Vocab::borrow in the test
# a_hundred_thousand_made_up_tokens_are_found_where_today_s_order_puts_them of vocabulary, a hundred thousand
# made-up tokens, on a debug server kernel (./build.sh --server) built with the siblings of DEPENDENCIES.lock, the test
# alone selected. The radix sort of the tokens' bytes holds it (LplAssistant#99); the insertion sort it replaced
# counted 81,857,478,043 instructions there, so a sort that turns quadratic again passes the budget a thousand times
# over. Locking LplAssistant at its ranked merges (#908) added 450,118 instructions, Vocab::borrow's pass that finds
# the longest token (LplAssistant#114): Vocab::borrow counts 700,063 of them for the hundred thousand tokens.
# Checked by tools/instructions.sh --budget tools/budgets/vocabulary-borrow.debug.budget kernel/lpl.kernel; a pull
# request that moves the lock records the new counts.
inside=lpl::infer::Vocab::borrow
times=1
append=lpl.test=vocabulary.a_hundred_thousand_made_up_tokens_are_found_where_today_s_order_puts_them
instructions=39989263
accesses=22276599
tolerance=1
